action.evin/git-release@v1.with.enabled.hover_plaintext:
enabled: ${release:bump.changed}

Conditional release (action.evin/git-release@v1.with.enabled): Skip the whole release when false.

Boolean or a template resolving to true or false; defaults to true. When false nothing is staged, committed, tagged, or pushed and committed is false.

action.evin/git-release@v1.with.push.hover_plaintext:
push: { force: true }

Publish refs (action.evin/git-release@v1.with.push): Push the branch and tag after committing.

Opt-in. A rejected push keeps the local commit and tag so it can be retried.

action.evin/review-request@v1.with.comma.hover_plaintext:
commands: { find: ..., create: ... }

Forge commands (action.evin/review-request@v1.with.commands): Shell commands that talk to the hosting provider.

Each command is an ESH string. Values reach commands through environment variables, never string interpolation. find is required.

action.evin/review-request@v1.with.conte.hover_plaintext:
context: { version: "${release:bump.version}" }

Command context (action.evin/review-request@v1.with.context): Extra values exposed to commands.

Keys may contain letters, digits, and underscores and become EVIN_REVIEW_CONTEXT_<KEY> variables, upper-cased.

action.evin/review-request@v1.with.wante.hover_plaintext:
wanted: ${release:bump.changed}

Request wanted (action.evin/review-request@v1.with.wanted): Whether a review request should exist.

Boolean or a template resolving to true or false; defaults to true. A wanted request is created or updated, an unwanted one is closed. title is required unless wanted is literally false.
